From: Orkhan Javadli <ojavadli@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 12:33:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/24] tei-v7 prompt-23: Cross-repository reconnaissance
 before solution commitment

---
 config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml | 2 +-
 tei/candidates.jsonl                  | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml b/config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml
index ce2c891..70d4d1e 100644
--- a/config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml
+++ b/config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ agent:
     Failure to follow these rules will cause your response to be rejected.
   instance_template: |
     <pr_description>
-    Consider the following PR description:
+    Consider the following PR description. Before choosing an implementation, treat the repository as authoritative: locate the affected module, its public entry points, nearby tests, CI or supported-version configuration, and the project's documented behavior. Do not transfer assumptions, APIs, exception choices, or test commands from other repositories; derive them from this checkout.
     {{task}}
     </pr_description>
 
diff --git a/tei/candidates.jsonl b/tei/candidates.jsonl
index 55c785f..f882fba 100644
--- a/tei/candidates.jsonl
+++ b/tei/candidates.jsonl
@@ -49,3 +49,4 @@
 {"version_id": "prompt-19", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Acceptance-contract and failing-reproduction gate", "target_failure_mode": "Incomplete or incorrect implementation on difficult issues", "expected_dimension": "execution_accuracy", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "sympy__sympy-19783", "django__django-16569", "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "sympy__sympy-15875", "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml", "find": "Treat this as a repository-specific maintenance task, not a generic coding exercise.", "replace": "Treat this as a repository-specific maintenance task, not a generic coding exercise. First convert the report into an explicit acceptance contract: identify the current behavior, the required behavior, affected call paths, and at least one minimal failing reproduction. Do not finalize after making a plausible edit; rerun the reproduction, add or run regression coverage for the contract, and inspec"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.9, "reasoning_soundness": 0.88, "execution_accuracy": 0.84, "output_integrity": 0.92}, "aggregate": 0.885, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-19783", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16569", "score": 0.93}, {"instance_id": "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "score": 0.38}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-15875", "score": 0.35}, {"instance_id": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602", "score": 0.37}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0375, "why": "The explicit acceptance contract and failing reproduction reduce premature or incomplete fixes, improving alignment and execution on difficult issues. Gains are limited because a minimal reproduction does not by itself ensure coverage of repository-specific edge cases."}
 {"version_id": "prompt-20", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Invariant-first implementation planning", "target_failure_mode": "Incomplete or incorrect implementation on difficult issues", "expected_dimension": "reasoning_soundness", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "sympy__sympy-19783", "django__django-16569", "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "sympy__sympy-15875", "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml", "find": "Before editing, identify the project's language and version constraints, test commands, module layout, public API conventions, and analogous fixes in history or neighboring code.", "replace": "Before editing, identify the project's language and version constraints, test commands, module layout, public API conventions, and analogous fixes in history or neighboring code. Then state the invariant that must hold before and after the change, enumerate every caller or code path that can observe it, and explain why the proposed change preserves existing behavior outside the reported case."}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.89, "reasoning_soundness": 0.9, "execution_accuracy": 0.85, "output_integrity": 0.92}, "aggregate": 0.89, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-19783", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16569", "score": 0.94}, {"instance_id": "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "score": 0.36}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-15875", "score": 0.34}, {"instance_id": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602", "score": 0.35}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0425, "why": "Invariant-first planning materially improves reasoning quality and caller coverage, with a modest execution benefit. It can become overly analytical and still depends on correctly identifying the invariant, so difficult edge cases improve only slightly."}
 {"version_id": "prompt-21", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Repository-specific edge-case test matrix", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient robustness across project-specific edge cases", "expected_dimension": "execution_accuracy", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "sympy__sympy-19783", "django__django-16569", "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "sympy__sympy-15875", "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml", "find": "Treat this as a repository-specific maintenance task, not a generic coding exercise.", "replace": "Treat this as a repository-specific maintenance task, not a generic coding exercise. Before implementation, construct a compact test matrix covering the reported case, the normal legacy path, empty or missing values, singleton and boundary values, malformed inputs with the project's expected exception type, repeated or stateful use, ordering and mutation effects, and any alternate backend or compa"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.85, "reasoning_soundness": 0.87, "execution_accuracy": 0.85, "output_integrity": 0.89}, "aggregate": 0.865, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-19783", "score": 0.94}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16569", "score": 0.93}, {"instance_id": "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "score": 0.43}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-15875", "score": 0.4}, {"instance_id": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602", "score": 0.41}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0175, "why": "The focused edge-case matrix is the strongest direct response to the weak probes and improves robustness across empty, singleton, boundary, and malformed inputs. It slightly reduces target alignment and output integrity because broad matrix construction can encourage scope expansion or brittle over-testing beyond the reported contract."}
+{"version_id": "prompt-22", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Behavioral compatibility and neighboring-pattern checkpoint", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient robustness across project-specific edge cases", "expected_dimension": "reasoning_soundness", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "sympy__sympy-19783", "django__django-16569", "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "sympy__sympy-15875", "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml", "find": "Before editing, identify the project's language and version constraints, test commands, module layout, public API conventions, and analogous fixes in history or neighboring code.", "replace": "Before editing, identify the project's language and version constraints, test commands, module layout, public API conventions, and analogous fixes in history or neighboring code. For each relevant neighboring implementation, compare input normalization, error handling, ordering, mutation, caching, and backend or version-specific behavior; follow the established convention unless the issue explicit"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.85, "reasoning_soundness": 0.83, "execution_accuracy": 0.77, "output_integrity": 0.89}, "aggregate": 0.835, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "score": 0.93}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-19783", "score": 0.92}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16569", "score": 0.91}, {"instance_id": "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "score": 0.31}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-15875", "score": 0.27}, {"instance_id": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602", "score": 0.33}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": -0.0125, "why": "Neighboring-pattern comparison can catch compatibility and behavioral inconsistencies, but it risks importing assumptions from superficially similar code. That overgeneralization lowers alignment and execution accuracy, with little benefit on the hardest repository-specific probes."}
